this is the soldier spending 10 days in  an Israeli Army prison Israeli activists  have gathered in the occupied West Bank  City of Hebron on a fact-finding trip  it became very violent very quickly the  soldiers have been suspended it's not  clear what other punishment the soldier  who threw the punches now faces but the  soldier who verbally abused one of the  activists has been jailed for 10 days  the activist asked if filming the  incident was against the law the soldier  responded I decide what the law is and  you are acting against the law he also  invokes the name of the man likely to be  Israel's new security minister Ultra  nationalist etmar Ben gevir saying Ben  gevir will make order here you've all  lost it all you do here is finished as  he walks away you can see the skull  patch on his uniform which says one shot  one kill No Remorse I decide Edmar Ben  Giver visited the family of the man  jailed he demanded the Army rethink the  punishment saying the sentence was not  right and inappropriate Edmar bengafir  was already a controversial choice for  the new role of national security  minister he has a conviction for  incitement and links to a group  described by both the U.S and the  Israelis as a terrorist organization now  he's being accused of dragging the  Israeli Army into a political role and  criticizing the leaders of an  organization you'll have to work with  very closely  Alan Fisher Al Jazeera West Jerusalem
 

